# Copy to ~/.config/sih/credentials.env and fill in. NEVER put real values here.
#   install -m 600 /dev/null ~/.config/sih/credentials.env
#
# This file is committed. ~/.config/sih/credentials.env is not, and lives outside
# the repo so that anything scanning the project directory cannot read it.

# --- Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (Sentinel-2, Phase 5 Level 3) ---
# Register a free account at https://dataspace.copernicus.eu , then generate S3 keys at
#   https://eodata-s3keysmanager.dataspace.copernicus.eu/   -> "Add Credentials"
# The SECRET KEY IS SHOWN ONCE. Copy it before closing the dialog.
# Pick a long expiry -- the dialog asks for one, and an expired key fails at the
# download leg in a way that looks like a service outage (O10).
#
# Why S3 and not the account password: the OData *catalogue search* needs no
# credentials at all (verified 2026-08-21: HTTP 200 unauthenticated). Only the
# download leg is protected. S3 keys are revocable without touching the account,
# so the account password is never stored. Do NOT add CDSE_USERNAME/CDSE_PASSWORD.
#
# NOT the Sentinel Hub OAuth flow: that dashboard was sunset 2026-03-20, and the
# Sentinel Hub Process API serves rendered imagery, not the SAFE products with the
# SCL band that Phase 5 Level 3 needs.
#
# S3 endpoint: https://eodata.dataspace.copernicus.eu   bucket: s3://eodata
CDSE_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
CDSE_S3_SECRET_KEY=

# --- DLR / EnMAP L2A (Phase 5 Level 2 -- part of the BACKGROUND POOL, plan 2.1) ---
# Register at https://sso.eoc.dlr.de/geoservice/selfservice/public/newuser?locale=en
# (email-verification flow), then confirm and set a password.
#
# Verified 2026-08-21 against the live service:
#   STAC search  https://geoservice.dlr.de/eoc/ogc/stac/v1/collections/ENMAP_HSI_L2A
#                -> HTTP 200, NO credentials needed
#   asset GET    https://download.geoservice.dlr.de/ENMAP/files/...
#                -> redirects to sso.eoc.dlr.de/eoc/auth/login  (EOC UMS, CAS)
#
# CAS is a username/password TICKET flow. There is no API token, which is why the
# earlier EOWEB_TOKEN variable was deleted instead of left blank forever.
#
# DANGER: an unauthenticated asset GET returns HTTP *200* with an HTML login page,
# not 401. Fetchers must validate CONTENT (see core/http_guard.py), never status.
DLR_USERNAME=
DLR_PASSWORD=
